            "review_text": "David B\nRayong, Thailand9085 contributions\n0\nStreet Food Epitomized\nAug 2018 • Family\nVietnam is famous for its street foods, and nothing epitomizes it more than Pho Ba Ga, on Bat Dan street in Hanoi's Old Quarter.\n\nWhile Pho Bo Ga is actually in a building, you sit on small red plastic chairs with your knees tucked under your chin, on the sidewalk as Hanoi's ever busy and noisy traffic jostles past just inches away.\n\nPho (pronounced \"fer\") is traditional Vietnamese soup, usually eaten for breakfast or lunch. \"\"Bo\" means beef, and \"Ga\" means chicken, so Pho Bo Ga offers either beef or chicken noodle soup.\n\nAt VND 50,000 a bowl, it is the best value lunch in town.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten August 29, 2018",
